WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.567
Precision.

2
00:00:01.867 --> 00:00:03.700
The metric of false alarm cost.

3
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.667
Precision asks one question.

4
00:00:06.967 --> 00:00:10.833
Of everything the model flagged as positive, how much really was?

5
00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:19.333
Optimize it when acting on a flag is expensive, like a spam filter junking real mail, or a fraud system blocking a good card.

6
00:00:20.533 --> 00:00:22.200
Let's count with a spam filter.

7
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.692
Look only at the flagged column.

8
00:00:24.692 --> 00:00:28.733
Forty real spam plus five good emails, so forty five flags.

9
00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:31.467
Forty of those forty five were truly spam.

10
00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:37.900
So precision is true positives, divided by true positives plus false positives.

11
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.333
The true positives are the real hits.

12
00:00:40.633 --> 00:00:43.230
The false positives are the false alarms.

13
00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:46.967
Forty over forty five is about zero point eight eight nine.

14
00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:50.233
In code, compute it by hand first.

15
00:00:50.533 --> 00:00:52.333
Forty over forty plus five.

16
00:00:52.633 --> 00:00:56.000
Then scikit-learn gives the same number from the predictions.

17
00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.100
A trap: precision can be gamed.

18
00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:03.708
Flag only your single most confident case, and precision can be perfect.

19
00:01:03.708 --> 00:01:09.333
It says nothing about the positives you never flagged, so always read it together with recall.

20
00:01:10.533 --> 00:01:11.900
Here is a real trade.

21
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.433
Each flagged planet gets expensive telescope follow up.

22
00:01:15.733 --> 00:01:19.442
At precision point seven, three in ten follow ups are wasted.

23
00:01:19.442 --> 00:01:25.400
So you raise the threshold from point five to point eight, and precision climbs to point nine two.

24
00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.767
The price is recall, which is next.

25
00:01:28.967 --> 00:01:29.698
Let's recap.

26
00:01:29.698 --> 00:01:32.867
Precision is true positives over everything flagged.

27
00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:35.333
It is the metric of false alarm cost.

28
00:01:35.633 --> 00:01:38.733
It sees only the flagged pile, so read it with recall.

29
00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:40.367
Next up: recall.
